# Maintainer: Jordan Bettcher <thebettcher@gmail.com>
#
# Electron 43 for powerpc64le. Packaging, install layout, GN args and
# system-library choices follow Arch's electron43 43.7.0-1
# (gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/electron43; its
# maintainers are credited below). The source tree does not: Arch fetches ~160
# git repositories and runs gclient hooks, which cipd cannot bootstrap on
# ppc64le. This recipe assembles the tree gclient would have produced from
# release archives instead, the way packages/chromium does.
#
# Source tree (electron/DEPS, v43.7.0):
#   src/                          Google's chromium-150.0.7871.222-lite tarball
#                                 + chromium-150.0.7871.222-250.patch, which
#                                 makes it the 150.0.7871.250 Electron pins
#                                 (reference/chromium-150 has the provenance)
#   src/electron                  electron v43.7.0          (tag archive)
#   src/third_party/electron_node nodejs/node v24.21.0      (DEPS node_version)
#   src/third_party/nan           nodejs/nan 675cefeb       (DEPS nan_version)
# Not fetched, and why: squirrel.mac, ReactiveObjC, Mantle (macOS only);
# engflow reclient-configs (Google remote execution); pyyaml (DEPS
# checkout_pyyaml=False); PGO profiles (chrome_pgo_phase=0 and
# v8_builtins_profiling_log_file="", as Arch does). No cipd downloads: gn is
# built from source as in packages/chromium; node, java, rustc and gperf come
# from the system.
#
# Patch order in prepare():
#   1. chromium-150.0.7871.222-250.patch
#   2. Electron's own series, patches/config.json, via electron-apply-patches.py
#   3. Arch electron43's Chromium patches (the reference/chromium-150 set),
#      then its two Electron/Node patches
#   4. swiftshader + ppc64le patches r3 from reference/chromium-150, with
#      packages/chromium's _power8_compat toggle behaviour
#
# Conflicts, and how they were resolved (every step trial-applied to a copy
# of the tree for both _power8_compat values before this recipe was written):
#   - Electron's 407 patches expect a git checkout; the tarball has no .git,
#     so Electron's `git am` script can't run. electron-apply-patches.py
#     applies the same series in the same order with `git apply`.
#   - 13 file diffs in 7 of those patches modify tests the -lite tarball
#     doesn't ship, and are excluded by path (the helper prints each one):
#       chromium/cherry-pick-cf1e39ed8884  blink web_tests expectations (3)
#       chromium/cherry-pick-3c3b9747e9c2  blink web_tests wpt (1)
#       chromium/cherry-pick-8ec00dde14f6  content/test/data, wpt (2)
#       v8/cherry-pick-2ef100a053c5        test/unittests (1)
#       v8/cherry-pick-b74028b55c          test/cctest (1)
#       v8/cherry-pick-7e94f5ffc104        test/mjsunit/mjsunit.status (1)
#       dawn/tint_msl_add_switchreturn_ir_transform  tint .msl expectations (4)
#     dawn/tint_minor_fixup_to_switchreturn_transform failed only because it
#     builds on the file the previous patch creates; with that one applied,
#     it applies unchanged.
#   - Arch runs `git -C electron cherry-pick -n 5b8ae0ab` (electron#52238,
#     GTK message-box theme). v43.7.0 already contains it; patch reports it
#     as previously applied. Dropped.
#   - Our Chromium and ppc64le patches after Electron's: no conflicts. Three
#     files are patched by both Electron and us (build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn,
#     third_party/blink/renderer/platform/BUILD.gn, v8/BUILD.gn), and every
#     patch still applies, POWER8 Force-baseline included.
#     chromium-150-fix-sysroot-path-error needs fuzz 2 on the Electron-patched
#     tree; the rest apply at offsets.
#
# Build-system fixes found by building (not patch conflicts):
#   - yarn install --mode=skip-build: electron/package.json opts @sentry/cli
#     back into install scripts, and its postinstall fetches a binary with no
#     ppc64 build (HTTP 403). No script-built npm package is used to build.
#   - override_electron_version: electron/BUILD.gn reads the version from
#     electron/.git, which a tag archive doesn't have.
#   - The whole build uses the recipe's own gn, built in prepare() the way
#     packages/chromium does. build() puts $srcdir/gn/out first on PATH, so
#     every gn call reaches it, including the `gn args` that Node's
#     generate_config_gypi.py runs by name partway through ninja (step
#     ~36,950 of 44,520). That call is how this came up.
#
# Node inside Electron is built by Electron's GN files (patches/node,
# build_add_gn_build_files.patch) against Chromium's //v8 and BoringSSL
# (build/args/all.gn: node_openssl_path). Node's own deps/v8 and deps/openssl
# per-arch configurations are therefore unused. node_arch follows target_cpu
# ("ppc64", which is process.arch), and nothing in those GN files gates ppc64
# out.
#
# Maintainer: Caleb Maclennan <caleb@alerque.com>
# Contributor: loqs <bugs-archlinux@entropy-collector.net>
# Contributor: kxxt <rsworktech@outlook.com>

pkgver=43.7.0
pkgrel=2
_major_ver=${pkgver%%.*}
pkgname="electron${_major_ver}"

_chromium_ver=150.0.7871.250
_tarball_ver=150.0.7871.222
_node_ver=24.21.0
_nan_commit=675cefebca42410733da8a454c8d9391fcebfbc2
# gn: the commit reference/chromium-150 builds with.
_gn_commit=27a549cc1f83b223cf07e152f3e36681d5dd68fd
# 150.0.7871.250's revision stamps (github.com/chromium/chromium tag, and DEPS).
_chromium_commit=f916f1b7136907af19d96b95b891533d091d932a
_chromium_commit_position=4305
_chromium_commit_time=1786991556
_skia_revision=9c7b2dffb2433f5a0cc2b77f06025a09126807ed
_dawn_revision=b8cea1289d76a80e877e0d751ef3a35088256e89

# ppc64le ISA level -- same switch, values and semantics as packages/chromium.
#   0 = POWER9 (ISA 3.0). THE DEFAULT IN THIS TREE.
#   1 = POWER8-legal (ISA 2.07), for Arch POWER's multi-architecture repo.
# Source stays POWER8-compliant either way; only compiler flags and
# build-system feature gates differ.
# Override per build:  _power8_compat=1 makepkg
_power8_compat=${_power8_compat:-0}

